{#
  The masthead: the wordmark and its chips on the left, the model's own
  definition on the right, closed by the spot rule.

  Shared by the hosted pages (layouts/base.njk) and the printable sheet
  (layouts/sheet.njk), which is why it is a partial rather than markup in the
  layout — the sheet is the printed form of the same block, and two copies
  would drift.

  `mastheadLede` decides whether the definition and the tagline show. The
  chrome carries the masthead on every page; only the pages that are *about*
  the model carry its definition.

  The status chip travels with the version, so it reaches the printed sheet
  too — where a reader has no site to check the caveat against. `status.note`,
  which says which part of the model is unfinished, is on the hosted index
  only.
#}
<header class="masthead">
  <div class="masthead-lockup">
    <a class="masthead-mark" href="{{ '/' | rel }}">
      <span class="wordmark">NAOMI</span>
      <span class="version-chip">v{{ matrix.version }}</span>
      <span class="version-chip version-chip--status">{{ matrix.status.label }}</span>
    </a>
    <p class="masthead-sub">{{ site.fullTitle }}</p>
  </div>
  {% if mastheadLede %}
  <div class="masthead-lede">
    <p class="lede-text">{{ matrix.definition }}</p>
    <p class="lede-note">{{ site.ledeNote }}</p>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="masthead-rule" aria-hidden="true"></div>
</header>
